<?php

/**
 * Function to sort an array in ascending or descending order using bubble sort algorithm
 * @param array $arr The array to be sorted
 * @param string $order The order in which the array should be sorted ("asc" or "desc")
 * @return array The sorted array
 */
function bubbleSort(array $arr, string $order = "asc"): array {
    $length = count($arr);
    // loop through each element of the array 
    // and compare it with the next element
    for ($i = 0; $i < $length - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = 0; $j < $length - $i - 1; $j++) {
            // check the order and compare the two adjacent elements accordingly
            if (($order == "asc" && $arr[$j] > $arr[$j + 1]) 
                || ($order == "desc" && $arr[$j] < $arr[$j + 1])) {
                // swap the elements if they are not in order
                $temp = $arr[$j];
                $arr[$j] = $arr[$j + 1];
                $arr[$j + 1] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }
    return $arr;
}

// get user input for array elements
$elements = readline("Enter array elements separated by space: ");
$arr = explode(" ", $elements);

// convert the elements to integers
$arr = array_map("intval", $arr);

// ask the user for the sort order
$order = strtolower(readline("Enter sort order (asc or desc) [Default is asc]: ") ?: "asc");

// sort the array
$arr = bubbleSort($arr, $order);

// display the sorted array
echo "Sorted array: " . Implode(", ", $arr) . PHP_EOL;
```

This code takes user input for an array of integers and asks for the sort order: ascending or descending. It then uses the bubble sort algorithm to sort the array in the specified order and outputs the sorted array. The `bubbleSort()` function is a reusable piece of code that takes an array and the sort order as input and returns the sorted array. The code uses proper formatting and comments to ensure good readability and maintainability of the code.
